  "interpretation": {
    "directly_supported": [
      "The 2022-12-07 publisher note specifies three Spear Goblins per wave, 0.5 seconds between members, a 29-second lifetime, a 10-second spawn frequency, and a published total of 12.",
      "The pinned raw fields agree on a 3-member periodic group, 500ms interval field, 10000ms pause field, 29000ms lifetime, and a 3-count SpearGoblin death-spawn record.",
      "The post-rework raw profile is unchanged between the 2022-12-07 and 2023-02-18 snapshots."
    ],
    "inference_only": [
      "If the publisher's total includes the raw death-spawn branch, then 12 = 9 periodic units + 3 death-spawn units, consistent with three periodic waves of three.",
      "For the old profile, 11 = 8 one-unit waves at 4-second cadence during a 31-second active lifetime + 3 death spawns is consistent with a zero-offset active-time schedule. This arithmetic supports, but does not prove, that schedule origin."
    ],
    "unresolved_questions": [
      "Does spawn_start_time=0 anchor to card input, end of deploy_time, start of lifetime, or another activation boundary?",
      "Does 10-second spawn frequency mean first-member-to-first-member cadence, or a pause after the preceding batch completes?",
      "Does the official total count include the death-spawn branch? The arithmetic strongly fits, but the note does not itemize its total.",
      "Does natural lifetime expiry use the same death-spawn branch as destruction? Does destruction cancel pending wave members or a scheduled next wave?",
      "What event/tick ordering applies if spawn, destruction, or expiry share a boundary? The 0-ms death_spawn_deploy_time field does not define processing order.",
      "The repository has no Goblin Hut reference clip to independently establish first-wave onset, member timing, cancellation, or expiry behavior."
    ]
